# 6. PROFESSIONAL SCALPING STRATEGY LIBRARY

Implement the following setup detectors using existing Phase 1–4 modules.

Each strategy must generate candidates through the existing centralized signal engine.

## Strategy 1 — Liquidity Sweep Reversal Scalp

### BUY

- Detect established sell-side liquidity.
- Price sweeps below the level.
- Price reclaims or rejects the level.
- Phase 2 candle psychology supports the reversal.
- Optional micro-MSS confirmation.
- Valid entry and risk conditions.

### SELL

- Detect established buy-side liquidity.
- Price sweeps above the level.
- Price rejects or reclaims below.
- Bearish candle confirmation.
- Optional micro-MSS.
- Valid entry and risk conditions.

Do not require all confirmations simultaneously if the selected setup variation permits an earlier valid entry.

## Strategy 2 — Micro-MSS Scalp

- Detect meaningful microstructure shift.
- Validate break relative to volatility.
- Use displacement or retest confirmation.
- Identify structural invalidation.
- Generate eligible directional candidate.

Support BUY and SELL.

## Strategy 3 — Order Block Rejection Scalp

- Locate active lower-timeframe OB.
- Track price return.
- Evaluate candle rejection.
- Confirm eligible setup.
- Avoid repeated signals from identical touches.

## Strategy 4 — FVG Retracement Scalp

- Detect confirmed FVG.
- Wait for valid retracement.
- Evaluate directional response.
- Determine entry eligibility.
- Avoid using an FVG created by future candles.

## Strategy 5 — Momentum Breakout Scalp

- Detect defined consolidation/high-low level.
- Confirm relevant breakout.
- Measure displacement.
- Analyze price acceptance and available follow-through.
- Produce candidate without chasing excessively extended candles.

## Strategy 6 — First Pullback Continuation

- Detect directional impulse.
- Identify first meaningful pullback.
- Analyze pullback depth.
- Confirm resumption.
- Generate trade candidate.

## Strategy 7 — Waterfall Continuation

- Reuse Phase 2 waterfall detection.
- Detect early momentum state.
- Identify valid continuation opportunity.
- Prevent repeated SELL signals for each bearish candle.
- Support equivalent bullish cascade entries.

## Strategy 8 — Compression Expansion

- Recognize narrow consolidation.
- Establish confirmed boundaries.
- Wait for meaningful breakout.
- Confirm appropriate continuation or retest.

## Strategy 9 — Failed Breakout Scalp

- Detect price moving beyond a relevant level.
- Recognize failed acceptance.
- Confirm reclaim.
- Evaluate reversal risk.
- Generate candidate in the opposite direction when justified.

## Strategy 10 — Breakout Retest

- Confirm breakout.
- Record broken level.
- Wait for eligible retest.
- Evaluate rejection/continuation.
- Issue candidate.

Keep each setup independently configurable.

Do not require all ten strategies to be enabled.

Do not generate multiple trade ideas for one underlying event just because several detectors identified it.

