## Bullish Cascade

Evaluate equivalent upward conditions.

## Entry timing

Allow a candidate near the earliest valid signal confirmation.

Do not wait for many additional bearish candles simply because more momentum evidence becomes available later.

Do not generate repeated entries from every candle in the same sequence.

## Avoid chasing

Reject or defer candidates when:

- Price is excessively extended relative to a defensible stop.
- Nearby opposing liquidity significantly limits reward.
- Momentum is weakening.
- Available reward-to-risk is inadequate.
- Spread or volatility makes the setup impractical.

An exhaustion warning must not automatically create an opposite-direction trade.

