# 9. PRECISION ENTRY PRICE ENGINE

Develop a consistent scalping entry model.

Each approved setup must determine:

- Direction.
- Entry type.
- Entry reference or zone.
- Confirmation timestamp.
- Eligibility time.
- Invalidation.
- Maximum acceptable entry distance.
- Setup expiration.
- Expected risk/reward based on the intended execution assumptions.

Support:

### Market-on-confirmation

An entry evaluated using the next realistically available execution price after confirmation.

### Limit entry

A defined price-zone entry that becomes eligible only if price reaches the level after the order could have been placed.

### Stop entry

A breakout entry triggered by a future eligible price crossing.

### Retest entry

An entry after a valid retest and confirmation.

Do not assume a limit order filled simply because a historical candle touched a level without considering execution assumptions.

Do not report a trade entered at the confirmation candle's earlier low/high if that price was unavailable when the signal was confirmed.

Separate signal detection from simulated execution.

No automatic real-money order placement in this phase.

